  "output": "I'll read README.md first to get the sentences, then create the page.Created `index.html` (358 bytes) with the title \"Ops scripts\" and a two-item list using the README descriptions: `deploy.bat` as the Windows deploy wrapper, `notes.txt` as the release checklist.\n\nShell output:\n\n```\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 358 Oct 22 03:14 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   0 Oct 22 03:14 shell_note.txt\n```\n\nTwo notes on how I ran it: I prefixed the command with `cd /workspace/project &&` because each bash call is a fresh subprocess and the working directory isn't guaranteed — the `touch ... && ls -l ...` portion is exactly as you specified. Also, `index.html` came out mode `600` while the existing repo files are `666`; if that matters for serving the page, `chmod 644 index.html` will align it.",
